course: dictionary
lesson: 8744
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word «service» is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask: what job is this word doing here?
explain: «Council tax is paid to the local council for local services such as bins, streetlights, roads and libraries.» Here a service is something the council provides to help people in the area.
explain: «Church is not only a Sunday service: there are Sunday school classes for children, youth groups for older ones, and camps and holiday clubs.» Here a service is a meeting for worship. The words church and Sunday tell you that.
explain: «Never pretend to be hurt, missing or in danger as a joke; it causes real fear and can waste emergency services' time.» Emergency services are the teams, such as police, fire and ambulance, who come quickly when someone calls for help.
fact: A service can be work that someone does for other people, such as a shop serving customers.
fact: A service can be a system that provides something people need, such as a bus service or the postal service.
fact: A service can be a check and repair of a car or machine, and to service something means to check and repair it.
fact: A religious service is a meeting for worship.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Council tax is paid to the local council for local services such as bins, streetlights, roads and libraries.» In this sentence, what does service mean? | A check and repair of a car | A church meeting for worship | *Things the council provides to help people | A game of tennis
exercise: «Church is not only a Sunday service: there are Sunday school classes for children.» What kind of service is a Sunday service? | A tennis serve | A quick meal in a café | *A meeting for worship | A check and repair of a car
exercise: «Never pretend to be hurt, missing or in danger as a joke; it causes real fear and can waste emergency services' time.» Which people are the emergency services? | Tennis players | *Police, fire and ambulance teams | Teachers and librarians | Shop workers who serve customers
test: The garage told Dad the car needed a service. What does service mean here? | A type of music | A bus route on a map | *A check and repair of a machine | A tennis point
test: «Streaming services such as Spotify are reported to pay roughly a fraction of a penny per play.» What is a streaming service? | A place where you go swimming | A religious meeting | *A system that provides music or films people can listen to or watch online | A kind of dog
exam: In a restaurant, good service means | The food is always cold | The tables are made of wood | *The staff are polite and quick to help | The menu has no prices
